    newFormula: "Height-Adjusted BMI = 1.3 × weight (kg) ÷ height²·⁵ (m²·⁵)",
    formulaExplanation: "Standard BMI divides weight by height squared (2D scaling). However, humans grow three-dimensionally (volume). The 2.5 exponent scaling factor compensates for height distortion, offering fairer scores for tall and short people.",
